                        "entry_id": "7078532a-a224-387c-abc0-1bbdf631aad2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Expressing the speaker’s wish for a given future event to occur, and also generally their emphasis on its contingency upon the divine will."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e1edff1d-a142-4e8f-891b-f8ec22630968",
                                "sense_id": "6ede42f0-0487-38fc-840c-3d540ac7ef52",
                                "text": "We will sign the contract tomorrow, inshallah."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae0d54ca-b6b1-4e90-abbe-185d885e2fcc",
                                "sense_id": "6ede42f0-0487-38fc-840c-3d540ac7ef52",
                                "text": "Hell yeah, from the river to the sea, Palestine must be, will be – inshallah – it will be free!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3a44d3f7-98ef-3e42-afa3-6f5a6353b9a3",
                        "entry_id": "7078532a-a224-387c-abc0-1bbdf631aad2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Expressing a skeptical affirmative, to indicate the unlikeliness of events, as if they need a divine intervention to come about."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial",
                            "sarcastic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
